• iPad: the app now runs natively on iPad in any orientation, with a wider home screen, a Settings sidebar and room for Stats. Split View, Slide Over and resizable windows work.
• Leaderboard and buddy streaks: posting from an iPhone or iPad should now work. Earlier builds were missing the App Attest permission the device check needs.
• Daily Dit: Copy now puts the result card image on the clipboard, with the text as a fallback, just like Share.
• Code Exam: you pass with one minute of solid copy at the exam's speed (25, 65 or 100 characters at 5, 13 or 20 WPM). Passages now include . , ? / and the AR, SK and BT prosigns, as on the real exams.
• Settings › Leaderboard & Buddy: a switch to hide the buddy line on the home screen.
Please try: the app on an iPad (rotate it, use it in a narrow window), posting a score to the leaderboard, pasting a copied Daily Dit card into Messages, and a Code Exam at 13 WPM.
